From ec24677f18b1f44d231062bbb28e9aebc84837d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ebg-ant <296364998+ebg-ant@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:30:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(presets): an arrangement of every display under a
 name
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`preset save [@display] [name]`, `preset load [@display] [--open] <name>`, `preset delete <name>` and
`presets` keep arrangements in a hand-editable presets.json: a name, and one line of the `layout`
notation for each display. From the menu (Presets), Go to…, shortcuts and links. One step for undo.
Names never reach the log or a trace.

Places of apps that are not open wait in the tree for three minutes, as saved slots wait after a launch
(Controller+WrittenSlots.swift). `layout --open` waits the same way: its own mechanism, which built the
tree again from the text, is gone. `applyLayout` becomes `arrange(_:open:wait:)`, which takes one line
per display and matches the slots of all of them in one pass.

Names of spaces are carried over by `reset(tree:carrying:)` like saved views.

Guide: docs/PRESETS.md. Spec: docs/features/F21-presets.md. Nothing of it has run on a Mac.
