diff --git a/collab/scenarios/F21-presets.sim b/collab/scenarios/F21-presets.sim
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..6b49ec4c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/collab/scenarios/F21-presets.sim
@@ -0,0 +1,102 @@
+# Story: a day. In the morning, on the laptop alone, the table is set by hand once and kept as "Solo".
+# A call comes in: another preset, whose notes app is not open yet and takes its place when it is. At the
+# desk a second display is plugged in and "Desk" arranges both at once. In the evening the laptop
+# is alone again and "Solo" brings the morning back.
+# Spec: F21. Window ids start at 101.
+open Safari
+open Terminal
+open Slack
+# Nothing is docked yet, so there is nothing to keep.
+preset save Solo
+expect fail
+dock 101 left
+dock 102 right
+dock 103 beside 102 bottom
+preset save Solo
+expect ok
+presets
+expect ok
+
+# A call: the call window large, notes beside it.
+open zoom.us
+open Notes
+layout zoom.us:2 | Notes
+expect ok
+preset save Call
+expect ok
+# Next time Notes is not open: its place is closed up, and waits.
+close 105
+float-all
+preset load call
+expect ok
+expect count docked 1
+expect docked 104
+expect floating 101
+# Looking around and docking something else meanwhile does not lose the place.
+zoom 104
+show-all
+dock 103 left
+open Notes
+expect docked 106
+expect left-of 104 106
+expect left-of 103 104
+expect count docked 3
+
+# A name that does not exist changes nothing.
+preset load Cal
+expect fail
+expect count docked 3
+
+# At the desk: a second display. One preset arranges both.
+displays 2
+layout @1 Safari | Terminal
+layout @2 Slack / Notes
+preset save Desk
+expect ok
+float-all
+preset load Desk
+expect ok
+expect count docked 4
+expect left-of 101 102
+expect above 103 106
+expect floating 104
+
+# The evening: the display is unplugged, and the morning's arrangement comes back.
+displays 1
+preset load Solo
+expect ok
+expect count docked 3
+expect left-of 101 102
+expect above 102 103
+expect floating 106
+expect camera root
+
+# A slot that nobody fills stops waiting: after the three minutes (flush runs them out) the app's window floats.
+close 103
+preset load Solo
+expect ok
+expect count docked 2
+flush
+open Slack
+expect floating 107
+expect count docked 2
+
+# Without a terminal: Save This Arrangement… in the menu runs `preset save`, which asks for the name on screen.
+preset save
+expect ok
+expect field open
+field-type --evening
+expect fail
+expect field open
+field-type Evening
+expect ok
+expect field closed
+float-all
+preset load evening
+expect ok
+expect count docked 2
+
+preset delete Call
+expect ok
+preset load Call
+expect fail
