+**Slots that wait** (`Controller+WrittenSlots.swift`). A slot that found no window waits the way a saved slot waits after launch (see "Persistence"): before the tree
+is built, the slot is filled with a stand-in number, which sits in the tree where the window belongs and takes no space. So the place moves with
+whatever the user does to the tree meanwhile, and the window that comes is swapped in with `replaceWindow`: the camera, history and saved views are not touched, and nothing jumps.
+`writtenSlots` maps each stand-in to the `WindowSlot` as written, and `WindowSlot.accepts` and `matchesTitle` decide who may take it; `claimPendingSlot`, called
+from `windowAppeared` before any rule, asks written slots first. Only a window that has just appeared is given one. `filledSlots` remembers which slot each window of the line has, so
+that a window that closes (a splash screen, an app being started again) leaves a stand-in behind. One timer (`written-slots`, three minutes) ends the wait everywhere, and moves nothing: it goes through `expireSlots`, so a place whose going would move a window stays, overdue, until the next layout that somebody causes; `arrange`, `float-all`,
+`layout` and `preset load` end it on their display (`forgetPendingSlots(on:)`), `shutdown()` (so also `pause`) everywhere. These stand-ins have no hint, so one that is saved in mid-wait is dropped by the next `reconcile()`.
+
+## Presets
+
+`preset save Desk`, `preset load Desk` (docs/PRESETS.md, docs/features/F21-presets.md). A preset is a name for one or more lines of the notation above, each perhaps beginning with its display (`@2 Slack | Mail`), so
+there is no second notation, matcher or launcher.
+
+- `Preset` and `PresetFile` (ArborCore) read the text of `presets.json` and change it. People write that file by hand, so it is treated as `settings.json` is: an entry that cannot be read is skipped with a reason, a change is made
+  to the text in one place (`JSONText`), and text that is not JSON is never rewritten.
+- `PresetStore` (Platform) only moves the text: `FilePresetStore` through `SettingsFile`'s reading and writing (links followed, permissions kept, read-only respected), `MemoryPresetStore` in ArborTesting. The file is read
+  whenever it is needed, so there is nothing to reload or to keep in step.
+- `Controller+Presets.swift`: saving writes what `layoutSpec(of:naming:waiting:)` gives for each display, with titles only for apps that have several slots; loading finds the display of each line and calls `arrange`.
+- `PresetMenu` (ArborCore) says what the menu's submenu holds; `presetSections()` makes rows of `MenuModel` of it, which `StatusMenu` draws like any others.
 
