Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(presets): what the presets file holds reaches neither
 the log nor a trace
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The two nets that know nothing of how words are hidden now put their word into every command for presets,
built in code in every shape, and into presets.json: as a name, in a title, where a display's number was
wanted, in a line that cannot be read, in a file that is no JSON. They found three leaks:

- "display word is not connected": a word of the file where a display's number was wanted. It is hidden in
  the log with the names, and gets a token in a trace, in replies and in the header's copy of the file.
- The reason an entry was skipped for can quote the line. The log and a trace get the place alone
  (`entry 3: column 9`), as of a file that cannot be read.
- `preset load @word`: as in `layout`, `…` in the log; in a trace the number of the display whose id it
  is, otherwise a token.

A command that cannot be read is written into a trace as the trunk writes any such command.

Scenario 54 answered for seven known jolts of `layout` (the line's own step moved a floating window a second
time, by the margin): they are mended, so the lines go.
