@@ -60,7 +60,9 @@ arborctl presets                     # what there is
 
 - A name is what follows the verb, words joined by one space: `preset save Deep Work`. Capitals are kept and do not count when looking a name up, nor does the kind or amount of space between words.
 - At most 40 characters (as names of spaces, F20), nothing invisible (as for names in the notation). A word cannot begin with `--` or `@`, which are options and displays.
-- **A name is never logged**, as names of spaces are not (F20): it may be a client or a project, and the log is what people paste into a bug report. The log has `preset load ‹name›: loaded ‹name›: arranged 3 windows`, and `entry 3` for an entry that was skipped. Of a file that cannot be read the reply quotes the text at the mistake, for whoever wrote it; the log and a trace get the place alone (`line 1, column 40`), as for settings.json.
+- **A name is never logged**, as names of spaces are not (F20): it may be a client or a project, and the log is what people paste into a bug report. The log has `preset load ‹name›: loaded ‹name›: arranged 3 windows`, and `entry 3` for an entry that was skipped. Of a file that cannot be read the reply quotes the text at the mistake, for whoever wrote it; the log and a trace get the place alone (`line 1, column 40`), as for settings.json. So it is with the reason an entry was skipped for (`entry 3: column 9`).
+- **A word where a display's number was wanted** (`preset load @word Desk`, or `"@word Slack"` in the file) is treated as in `layout`: `…` in the log, in a trace the display's number if it is one's id, otherwise a token. A command that cannot be read reaches a trace as no more than its first word, if that is one of Arbor's.
+  The nets that know nothing of how words are hidden (`CanaryTests`) put their word into every preset command and into the file. In the place of an app's name a word is an app's name, as in `layout`.
 - In a URL the words are separated by slashes: `arbor://preset/load/Deep/Work`. So a slash counts as a space, in the file too.
 
